        <p>I.—The first coupon is free, and no competitor can send in more thim one free coupon, Enclose Id. stamp for every . othdr coupon used. One postal Order must be enclosed if all the coupons on above sheet are used. Any number of coup ins an be sent in if paid for at the rate of One Shilling for each 20. 2.—Cross all Post 11 Orders and keep the numbers. 3.—No competitor can take more than one share of the £lO prize. 4.—The coupons must be forwArdel to the Bxaminer Office Warrington, the envelope to Ise' endorsed Football Coupon." so as to be delfrered by the first post on Thursday morning. If the envelope bears WeAuesday's postm4rk. it will be received up to 5 p.m. on Thursday. Coupons delivered by hand must be received not later than 9 a.m. on Thursday. s.—ComP4itors demAnding a scrutiny must enclose fee of Ten Shillings, give number of Postal Order (if any), and num- ber of couwins sent. In the event of the claim proving corrrt the fef- will be returned. 6.—ln the event of two or more competitors tying, prize money will be divided. 7.—A1l attempts in this competition must be made on coupons cut from this paper. B.—When not less than 40 attempts are made, the coupons of unsuccessful competitors for the coupon prize will be carried forward and added to the number sent in in the next competition, so that sooner or later the coupon prize must be won by regdlar competitors. 9.—The results will appear in the first issue following the result of the matches.</p>
