      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-09-29_WidnesExaminer_art0083" n="art0083">
        <head>RUNCORN PETIT SESSIONS.</head>
        <p>RUNCORN PETIT SESSIONS.</p>
        <p>MONDAY.—Before Messrs. W Timmins (presiding), and John Ockleston, AN ANXIOUS CycLisr.—Percy Hilton, o! Duke's Fields, was summoned for riding his bic•-cle in Halton-roa4, at 10-45 on the 23rd August. witbout a light.—P.C. Fry, stated he was in Halton-road at the time, and saw the defendant go by on his machine having no light. He called to him to stop but he did not, Witness was then Oligod to follow him. Defec.- dant then get off his machine, and witness asked him why he did not stop on being called to the first time? Defendant re- plied He wanted to get horne."—Defendant stated the constables story was correct. All he wished to say was that the officer being in plain clothes at the time he did nqt know it was a constable that. was calling 10 him- else he would have etopped.—Mr. Ockleston Yon know you oug,hl. 10 ,always stop if you are asked to. Whoever setts you I—Defendant looked surprised.—Fined 103 including casts, Ca:' aaya in default. PLAYING CARDS BY MooNLElßT.—Willtattv litohth, 'George ‘• -1-' •.ttO! :I :1 • • • • ; „•• • • •</p>
