        <p>THE DISASTER AT DARJEELING. 400 LIVES LOST.</p>
        <p>The Lieutenant-Governor ot Bengal wired on Wednes- day night ; "No written details ye':, from Darjeeling, and telegraphic accounts cinfused, but loss of life probably amounts to the melancholy number of 400. About 300 soldiers are manfully helping the civil authorities. Railway track and ,road still blocked, but telegraph restored.</p>
